{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1559699-real-or-fictional-city","id":1559699,"title":"Real or fictional city","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-05-02T06:49:16-07:00","id":1559699,"title":"Real or fictional city","content":"I was wondering what everybody's experience and preference is. Do you usually set your games in real life cities (and if so, which, how do you choose?) or fully fictional ones?<br /> <br /> Usually, when I prepare a chronicle, I tend to go towards picking real life cities, usually set in europe with a long history (like Rome, Constantinople, London, Paris, Marseille). I feel Vampire really lends itself well to incorporating local myths and legends. And as a Storyteller I really like the research aspect of preparing and reading up on a local city and its history.<br /> <br /> However, worldbuilding-wise, I really enjoy the flexiblity that creating a city from imagination would offer, but in practise i haven't done so that often. What are your experiences/thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7279-ichneumon","name":"Ichneumon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7279_6.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-03T07:53:22-07:00","id":1559721,"title":"","content":"As of yet I used always real cities, often using real maps where possible. In the city where my group and I live also. I like a game as Vampire to have somehow real-life roots where player can recognize places and lifestyle.<br /> It may happen that some small town or location could be invented though, especially it not planned as part of the main setting.<br /> <br /> So far, the main setting we have played in, were: Modern Rome, Ancient Rome, Medieval Costantinople. Some short story in Victorian London.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-04T14:49:46-07:00","id":1559771,"title":"","content":"ALWAYS FICTIONAL!!! That way, I can create the city the way I want to.<br /> <br /> But, I always base the city off of familiar allusions (from a writing-guide book I have from 1921);<br /> <br /> Los Angeles = City of Angels<br /> Baltimore = Monument-City<br /> New York = Gotham-City<br /> Liberty City = Generic for any city back East. (I've never played GtA, but, it's a good name).<br /> London = Lonton<br /> Buenos Aires = Valentina<br /> <br /> And it's not the name of the city used, but when, it's used. I've been working on a southern-city using Civ3 graphics for years now that, I was inspired by visiting Jekyll Island, Ga, and thought: &quot;What if I had an island, full of the wealthy, right next to an industrial-city&quot;. It takes years, because I keep getting better ideas and redoing what I've done.<br /> <br /> Edit: for Dark Ages, nothing beats my War Times level-editor; I can literally make the map, at night, and use the graphics to create a Medieval-city or 1930's era American or European-Town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 05-04-2026, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T21:26:01-07:00","id":1559797,"title":"","content":"I started with fictional cities but eventually just pivoted to real life ones. It takes a lot of the burden off me for having to explain the relevance of everything and if you're just going to use analogs, like 'the Prince operates in the Imperial State building, it's like the Empire State building,' why not use the original? You don't have to be a geographer or follow the news to know the basics of New York City or Los Angeles or other areas that have been portrayed in media, or obviously the place that the group lives in. If you live in Elfers you know you're not even in a town, you're in a 'census designated place.' But if the players are in San Canyonero I'll have to either write up a file for them to read or hold their hand throughout the whole thing so that when they go to a meeting at the Statue of Dependence they know whether it's some ten foot tall thing or over a hundred and fifty with its own dedicated island.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-05T23:17:36-07:00","id":1559799,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer using real world cities for the World Of Darkness myself and use fictional cities for games like StarFinder, Phase World or Aliens Unlimited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-12T10:33:10-07:00","id":1559901,"title":"","content":"Prefer real life cities, but fictionalized to fit my needs where necessary- I think everyone understands the details are not 1-to-1 in a world with vampires, mummies etc.<br /> I do however prefer American cities (because that means my players won't be familiar with them), and I have a faible for cities that are nearby big shots, but themselves not as huge (e.g. Suffolk, Williamsburg, Cape Charles instead of Virginia Beach, Phoenixville, Doylestown or Pottstown instead of Philly, Kingston instead of NYC etc).<br /> I like this because I want to be able to have a more 'rural' feel but still be in proximity to huge cities. Allows for 'natural progressions' of outgrowing the local battlefield and moving up to &quot;the big league&quot; (which can be a natural chronicle end/break). And I use places that are not as known, making things easier for me to handwave/adapt.<br /> I also like using real world maps in e.g. google and setting up territorites etc.<br /> <br /> Plus I like researching stuff about real world cities. Learning as a neat side effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8542,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","user":"Wormwood","date":". 05-12-2026, 02:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-05-13T07:33:36-07:00","id":1559920,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking about this yesterday as I contemplate restarting older games, timeskipping to the present. The more remote towns were mostly fictional, as back in the 1990s it was hard/slow to find that kind of information but the big cities were fictionalized versions based on the Rage Across... book we used as a baseline. My thoughts yesterday were a bit broader though, in using entire alternate histories for the CoD, for example, take the HoI4 mod Kaiserreich as the baseline history for the world. I might give this a go for a smaller/solo game to see how it works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T15:43:44-07:00","id":1560537,"title":"","content":"For VtR (and VtM) I use real cities. That gives me a wealth of history to draw upon for ideas and other things that I can use as needed. Plus it gives me the sort of restrictions that allows for my creativity to flourish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13674-amalasuintha","name":"Amalasuintha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13674_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T07:06:45-07:00","id":1560582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amalasuintha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1559699-real-or-fictional-city?p=1560537#post1560537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For VtR (and VtM) I use real cities. That gives me a wealth of history to draw upon for ideas and other things that I can use as needed. Plus it gives me the sort of restrictions that allows for my creativity to flourish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly the same. Time is a character of its own in vampire games, so going near-historical novel with the past of an actual place, with some folklore &amp; urban legends projected through the lens of the setting used, just feels natural to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T09:42:15-07:00","id":1560583,"title":"","content":"Fictional city saves me the headache of having to do additional research! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T12:12:25-07:00","id":1560584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1559699-real-or-fictional-city?p=1560583#post1560583\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fictional city saves me the headache of having to do additional research! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, it's more like substitution. Using a real place means less time spent thinking up a lot of the incidental details of a fake city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T22:18:44-07:00","id":1561276,"title":"","content":"Both, depends on the game. Some stories lend themselves better to one or the other.<br /> <br /> There's also a third option: fictional, but not yours. Things like Gotham (from Batman) or Arkham (from Lovecraft, not Batman).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-18T01:09:17-07:00","id":1564161,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t know any real cities well enough for them to be anything but a fictional city with a real world map so I just use fictional cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-09-19T19:35:13-07:00","id":1564204,"title":"","content":"I may have already posted this, but it's relevant for city-building:<br /> <br /> <img width=\"700\" height=\"584\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://img-9gag-fun.9cache.com/photo/an9X6Zz_700bwp.webp\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://img-9gag-fun.9cache.com/photo/an9X6Zz_700bwp.webp\" data-thumb-url=\"https://img-9gag-fun.9cache.com/photo/an9X6Zz_700bwp.webp\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}